{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01TO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\colim \\Mor_S(T_i, X) = \\Mor_S(\\lim T_i, X)\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$T_i$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$S = \\lim_i S_i$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$X_i$", "MATH_0008": "$S_i$", "MATH_0009": "$i$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{limits-proposition-characterize-locally-finite-presentation}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{limits-section-descending-relative}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTBFCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTBFOPEN_0001": "{\\bf "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d7ffb38ba6ef931b8abf88a5c0723b73985d2268e435765b8d019e2302e8b777", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a1225b1c33bd5518e70432678e1f45c449fc8780a873e1fa2735025c5b7534e4", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNote that a morphism of finite presentation is <TEXTBFOPEN_0001>not<TEXTBFCLOSE_0001> just a quasi-compact\nmorphism which is locally of finite presentation.\nLater we will characterize morphisms which are\nlocally of finite presentation as those morphisms such that\n<MATH_0001>\nfor any directed system of affine schemes <MATH_0002> over <MATH_0003>. See\nLimits,\nProposition <REF_0001>.\nIn Limits, Section <REF_0002> we show\nthat, if <MATH_0004> is a limit of affine schemes,\nany scheme <MATH_0005> of finite presentation over <MATH_0006> descends to a scheme\n<MATH_0007> over <MATH_0008> for some <MATH_0009>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c493c443bfbb6272320263c7a2ee7db72cc845f96ee4164ee89bf15d6e655519", "unit_id": "tag:01TO:prose-0002"}
